---
layout: article
title: Chat with the Agent
description: Open the Appwrite Agent panel or fullscreen chat, send prompts, and manage a conversation.
---

Chat is the primary way you use the Appwrite Agent. You can work in a side panel while staying on a Console page, or open the fullscreen Agent for longer sessions.

# Open the Agent {% #open-the-agent %}

### Right-hand panel

1. Sign in to [Appwrite Cloud](https://cloud.appwrite.io).
2. Click the **Agent** control in the Console header.
3. The Agent panel opens on the right. Your panel open state can persist in account preferences.

### Fullscreen

1. Go to `/agent` (or `/agent/{conversationId}` for a specific thread).
2. Use the conversation list, composer, settings, and automations from the dedicated Agent shell.

{% info title="Keyboard shortcuts" %}
The Console includes shortcuts to create a new agent conversation, create an automation, and focus the composer. Open the shortcuts dialog from the Console for the current key bindings.
{% /info %}

# Start or continue a conversation {% #start-or-continue %}

1. Click **Create agent** for a new thread, or select an existing conversation.
2. Optionally choose a [model](/docs/products/agent/models) from the model picker.
3. Type a prompt, pick a suggestion chip, or use voice input.
4. Optionally attach files before sending.
5. Send the message and watch the reply and tool timeline update live.

# Work with a turn {% #work-with-a-turn %}

While the Agent is working:

- **Stop** cancels an in-progress run when the conversation is locked for a turn.
- **Retry** asks the Agent to try the turn again after a failure or stop.
- **Edit and resend** changes a prior user message and continues from there.
- **Clarify** prompts may appear; answer them to continue the same turn.

After a reply, you can copy text, use text-to-speech, or leave thumbs up / thumbs down feedback.

# Tips for better results {% #tips-for-better-results %}

- Stay on the project or page you mean before asking project-specific questions.
- Be specific: include resource names, error text, or the outcome you want.
- Connect [Appwrite MCP](/docs/products/agent/connect-mcp) when you want the Agent to list or change resources.
- Save standing preferences in [memory](/docs/products/agent/memory) instead of repeating them every chat.

